<!--BlockML Documentation — import A02 data into A03
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task.A03_02_CopyData-->
<task:A03_02_CopyData xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that imports A02 data into A03
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A03 authoring task: wipe a03_authoring.data, copy the full
    a02_structuring.data tree into it, then remap packages and names
    so the imported Blocks live only in A03.

    - **Wipe** — delete the live A03 data package before the copy.
      Leftover ignored trees (for example data_IGNORE) are not input
    - **Copy** — the whole A02 data package, not individual DocSet /
      Page / PageGroup sync
    - **Remap** — one pass after the copy: A02 packages and sector
      names become A03; no A03 file may reference another sector
    - **Sources** — this task has no authoritativeSources
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          Import the complete A02 data package into A03. Do not sync
          individual DocSets, Pages, or PageGroups. Do not read
          authoritativeSources on this task. Do not read BmlDocSetPlan.
          Do not edit A02. Do not write outside a03 data. Do not invent
          files that are not in A02 data.

          Source package: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data
          Source path:
          packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a02_structuring/data/

          Target package: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data
          Target path:
          packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a03_authoring/data/

          Leave a03_authoring/task, a03_authoring/example, and
          A03_AuthoringSector untouched. PageExample_A03 is not data.

          1. Delete live A03 data
          Delete the entire live A03 data tree (the target path above)
          including every descendant package (data.page, data.pagegroup,
          data.page.docs, and any other child). Delete every .bml file
          in that tree. Remove those A03 data Blocks from
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library. Do not remove A02 catalog
          entries, task entries, PageExample_A03, or other sectors.

          Ignore leftover non-package trees such as
          a03_authoring/data_IGNORE. They are not live A03 data. Do not
          read them, copy from them, or merge them. If they still hold
          old A03 files, do not treat those files as the current set.

          After this step A03 has no live data Blocks.

          2. Copy the full A02 data tree
          Copy every file and subdirectory from the A02 data path into
          the A03 data path, preserving relative paths. Example:
          a02_structuring/data/page/docs/Intro.bml
          → a03_authoring/data/page/docs/Intro.bml
          a02_structuring/data/pagegroup/RootPageGroup.bml
          → a03_authoring/data/pagegroup/RootPageGroup.bml
          a02_structuring/data/BmlDocSet_A02.bml
          → a03_authoring/data/BmlDocSet_A02.bml
          (the DocSet file name is remapped in step 3).

          Copy the complete tree once. Do not filter pages vs groups vs
          the DocSet. Do not skip a file because an older A03 copy
          existed. There is no older live A03 copy after step 1.

          3. Remap packages and names (one pass)
          After the copy, every imported file still names A02. Rewrite
          each imported file so it is an A03 Block. Apply these
          substitutions everywhere they appear — xmlns URIs, root
          element names, FQN comments, see-links, property values,
          TypeReference tokens, and prose that identifies this Block's
          sector:

          - package prefix
            org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data
            → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data
          - filesystem segment a02_structuring/data
            → a03_authoring/data (comments / examples only)
          - Block name BmlDocSet_A02 → BmlDocSet_A03
          - file BmlDocSet_A02.bml → BmlDocSet_A03.bml
            (rename the file; do not leave the A02 file name)
          - wording that says this Block is A02 / a02 / structuring
            data becomes A03 / a03 / authoring data

          Page and PageGroup Block names stay the same (Intro,
          RootPageGroup, …). Only the package and the DocSet name
          change.

          After the remap, an A03 file may reference only:
          - other A03 data Blocks (the remapped counterparts)
          - lib / docgen / core types (for example
            org.blockml.bml.documentation.*, org.blockml.bml.docgen.*)

          An A03 file must never reference a Block from another sector
          (a01_planning, a02_structuring, a04_rendering, or any later
          sector). Drop or remap such a reference. Do not keep an A02
          FQN because "the A03 counterpart is missing" — the counterpart
          is the remapped copy in this same import.

          Do not change A02 files. Do not change files outside the
          imported A03 data tree.

          4. Confirm the imported set
          The live A03 data package must contain the same relative
          files as A02 data, with packages and the DocSet name remapped.
          BmlDocSet_A03.pages, pageGroups, homePage, and rootPageGroup
          list only A03 Blocks. Each PageGroup parentGroup, pages, and
          landingPage list only A03 Blocks. See-links between imported
          Blocks point at A03 counterparts.

          5. Export imported A03 data from the catalog
          Export every Block under
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data (including
          descendants) from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is
          not already in the catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of
          other sectors. Do not remove PageExample_A03 if it is
          catalogued.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
</task:A03_02_CopyData>
